{"text": "2025-04-02 16:28:11.292 | INFO     | app.api.v1.reports:generate_report:128 - Report would appear in list as: {'id': 'e43ee694-31bf-407e-9465-bc1cf337fa3e', 'title': 'Email Content Report', 'report_type': 'weekly_ops', 'status': 'complete', 'summary': 'This is an example of a weekly operations report for Amazon, based on an email received from Amazon regarding a return request for an item purchased on their platform. The report includes the following sections:\\n\\n* Facts: Provides details on the item being returned, including the quantity and the item name.\\n* Operational Data: Offers information on the email\\'s origin, such as whether it was sent from a notification-only address that cannot accept incoming email. It also mentions any limitations of the email, such as the lack of information on how to handle returns for items without pre-printed return labels or how to track the status of the return after drop-off at UPS Dropoff locations.\\n* Upcoming Priorities: Suggests ways to improve the efficiency of Amazon\\'s return process, such as providing options for customers to track the status of their returns through either \"Your Orders\" or \"Your Returns\" (if it exists).\\n* Recommendations: Offers suggestions on how to enhance customer satisfaction and loyalty, such as providing information on how to handle returns for items without pre-printed return labels or how to track the status of the return after drop-off at UPS Dropoff locations.\\n\\nThe report is intended to provide a summary of Amazon\\'s operations and identify areas that may require improvement.', 'created_at': '2023-04-15T10:30:00Z', 'data_sources': ['gmail']}\n", "record": {"elapsed": {"repr": "0:06:15.018362", "seconds": 375.018362}, "exception": null, "extra": {}, "file": {"name": "reports.py", "path": "C:\\Users\\scott\\Desktop\\Echo\\EverRaise\\backend\\app\\api\\v1\\reports.py"}, "function": "generate_report", "level": {"icon": "ℹ️", "name": "INFO", "no": 20}, "line": 128, "mes